    <a class="press-item" id="leo" href="/conferences/"><img src="/images/emblem-holy-see.svg" alt="" style="max-height:64px"><div><h3>The medal of Pope Leo XIV's first year</h3><p class="meta">Presented by Archbishop Gabriele Caccia, Apostolic Nuncio to the United States · Washington, July 14, 2026</p><p>Sent by the Holy Father to the founder of the Orientale Lumen Conferences on the occasion of the thirtieth. The medal commemorates the 1700th anniversary of the Council of Nicaea and bears Christ's prayer <em>ut mundus credat</em>, that the world may believe.</p></div></a>
    <a class="press-item" id="koch" href="/conferences/"><img src="/images/emblem-holy-see.svg" alt="" style="max-height:64px"><div><h3>Address of Cardinal Kurt Koch to Orientale Lumen XXX</h3><p class="meta">Prefect, Dicastery for Promoting Christian Unity · Rome, July 15, 2026</p><p>"Becoming a common heritage could be the definition of reception. In a sense, this Orientale Lumen Conference is also part of this reception process." The Cardinal also sent a personal message to Orientale Lumen XXIII in 2019, on the theme "One City, One Bishop."</p></div></a>
    <a class="press-item" href="https://www.ewtnnews.com/world/us/omalley-pace-speak-conference"><img src="/images/logo-ewtn.svg" alt="EWTN News"><div><h3>Cardinal O'Malley at Catholic-Orthodox conference: "Come together and pray for unity"</h3><p class="meta">EWTN News · July 2026</p><p>National coverage of the thirtieth conference, the Cardinal's keynote, and the vespers he prayed with Archbishop Pace and Metropolitan Tikhon.</p></div></a>
    <a class="press-item" href="https://www.catholicworldreport.com/2026/07/17/catholic-orthodox-bishops-join-in-dialogue-and-prayer-at-washington-d-c-conference/"><img src="/images/logo-cwr.png" alt="Catholic World Report"><div><h3>Catholic, Orthodox bishops join in dialogue and prayer at Washington conference</h3><p class="meta">Catholic World Report · July 2026</p><p>Report on the thirtieth conference: Archbishop Pace, Metropolitan Tikhon, Cardinal O'Malley, Bishop Vrame, and Bishop Botean. "I grew up with, I lived with, the tension between East and West my whole life," Jack Figel told the press.</p></div></a>
    <a class="press-item" href="https://www.catholicworldreport.com/2013/07/16/grassroots-ecumenism-of-friendship-keeps-orthodox-catholic-hopes-alive/"><img src="/images/logo-cwr.png" alt="Catholic World Report"><div><h3>Grassroots ecumenism of friendship keeps Orthodox-Catholic hopes alive</h3><p class="meta">Catholic World Report · July 2013 · Reprinted by Orthodox Christian Laity</p><p>A profile of the conferences at their seventeenth year: how they began, who has spoken, and why candid conversation happens here that cannot happen in the official dialogue.</p></div></a>
    <a class="press-item" href="https://catholicexchange.com/orientale-lumen-a-conference-rooted-in-heaven/"><img src="/images/logo-ce.png" alt="Catholic Exchange"><div><h3>Orientale Lumen: a conference rooted in heaven</h3><p class="meta">Catholic Exchange · May 2009</p><p>"There is no political agenda involved. These conferences offer face-to-face interaction without the need for official reports and studies. That is a benefit to all the Church and ultimately benefits the formal dialogue between Churches." Jack Figel</p></div></a>
